# Pairs with HandOffBound. Moved from the design's
# ReadPositionHonestRestampDuringClose. The close re-claims and records the heads
# first, and closes the intent and L's marker only afterwards (CloseMark), while
# the open check reads the marker. A walk rejected by the re-claim asks in
# between, is told "open", re-stamps with the post-close generation, and is
# allocated above the recorded heads.
MODULE: HandOffBoundRestampDuringClose
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the intent is marked closed only after the close's re-claim, so a rejected walk re-stamps with the post-close generation
PERTURBS: Close, GRestamp

--- FIND
Close ==
    /\ hoOpen
    /\ ~closing
    /\ fEpoch < MaxEpoch
    /\ fAdmit' = FALSE
    /\ fEpoch' = fEpoch + 1
    /\ fFence' = fEpoch + 1
    /\ hoClosedAt' = next
    /\ hoOpen' = FALSE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, author, windows, fpend, fkind, fstamp, restarted>>
    /\ UNCHANGED <<gst, gstamp, closing, gate, hfly, resumed, mInit>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the close re-claims first; CloseMark closes the intent and marker later.
Close ==
    /\ hoOpen
    /\ ~closing
    /\ fEpoch < MaxEpoch
    /\ closing' = TRUE
    /\ fAdmit' = FALSE
    /\ fEpoch' = fEpoch + 1
    /\ fFence' = fEpoch + 1
    /\ hoClosedAt' = next
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, author, hoOpen, windows, fpend, fkind, fstamp, restarted>>
    /\ UNCHANGED <<gst, gstamp, gate, hfly, resumed, mInit>>

CloseMark ==
    /\ closing
    /\ closing' = FALSE
    /\ hoOpen' = FALSE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, author, hoClosedAt, windows, fAdmit, fpend, fkind, fstamp, fEpoch, fFence, restarted>>
    /\ UNCHANGED <<gst, gstamp, gate, hfly, resumed, mInit>>
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ gst = "rejected"
    /\ hoOpen
    /\ ~closing
    /\ gst' = "repend"
--- REPLACE
    /\ gst = "rejected"
\* MUTATION: the open check reads the marker, not the intent's closing mark.
    /\ hoOpen
    /\ gst' = "repend"
--- END

--- FIND
    \/ GRestamp

--- REPLACE
    \/ GRestamp
    \/ CloseMark

--- END
